    "text": "(i) When <math><mn>0</mn></math> is at unit place <br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/68e6195f-153c-4d7f-8e97-440820028b42.png\" style=\"width:2.11319in;height:0.62639in\"> <math><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn></math>  <br/>(ii) When <math><mn>0</mn></math> is not at unit place <br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/6e0eedcb-ec6e-4ac1-a8f2-9509b732cec2.png\" style=\"width:2.11319in;height:0.63333in\"> <math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>96</mn></math>  <br/>(First fill unit place by either <math><mn>2</mn></math> or <math><mn>4</mn></math> i.e. two ways. Since we can not put <math><mi>‘</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>’</mi></math> at the thousand place it can be filled in <math><mn>4</mn></math> ways, remaining as usual) <br/>Total ways <math><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>96</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>156</mn></math>",
